      "bg": "navy",
      "caption": "Logic gates in one slide. 🔌📌\n\nShortcut: NAND and NOR are just AND and OR with the answer flipped.",
      "hashtags": [
        "olevelcs",
        "igcsecs",
        "computerscience",
        "logicgates",
        "booleanlogic",
        "cheatsheet"
      ],
      "slides": [
        {
          "layout": "formula",
          "eyebrow": "computer science · save this 📌",
          "title": "Logic gates, decoded",
          "cells": [
            {
              "name": "NOT",
              "f": "Q = NOT A",
              "note": "flips the input"
            },
            {
              "name": "AND",
              "f": "Q = A AND B",
              "note": "1 only if both inputs are 1"
            },
            {
              "name": "OR",
              "f": "Q = A OR B",
              "note": "1 if at least one input is 1"
            },
            {
              "name": "XOR",
              "f": "Q = A XOR B",
              "note": "1 if the inputs are different"
            },
            {
              "name": "NAND",
              "f": "Q = A NAND B",
              "note": "= NOT (A AND B): 0 only if both inputs are 1"
            },
            {
              "name": "NOR",
              "f": "Q = A NOR B",
              "note": "= NOT (A OR B): 1 only if both inputs are 0"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cs-08-indices",
      "bg": "lime",
      "caption": "The laws of indices. 📌 Seven rules, and the last three are where the marks are.\n\nNegative power = flip it. Fraction power = root it.",
      "hashtags": [
        "olevelmaths",
        "igcsemaths",
        "indices",
        "maths",
        "cheatsheet",
        "algebra"
      ],
      "slides": [
        {
          "layout": "formula",
          "eyebrow": "maths · save this 📌",
          "title": "Laws of indices",
          "cells": [
            {
              "name": "multiply → add",
              "f": "a^{m} × a^{n} = a^{m+n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "divide → subtract",
              "f": "a^{m} ÷ a^{n} = a^{m−n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "power of a power",
              "f": "(a^{m})^{n} = a^{mn}"
            },
            {
              "name": "power zero",
              "f": "a^{0} = 1"
            },
            {
              "name": "negative = flip",
              "f": "a^{−n} = {1 // a^{n}}"
            },
            {
              "name": "fraction = root",
              "f": "a^{1/n} = ⁿ√a"
            },
            {
              "name": "both at once",
              "f": "a^{m/n} = (ⁿ√a)^{m}",
              "note": "e.g. 8^(2/3) = (∛8)² = 2² = 4",
              "wide": true,
              "bg": "sun"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cs-09-trigonometry",
      "bg": "lilac",
      "caption": "Trig, all in one place. 📐📌\n\nRight angle? SOH CAH TOA. No right angle? Sine rule or cosine rule. That one question decides which half of this sheet you need.",
      "hashtags": [
        "olevelmaths",
        "igcsemaths",
        "trigonometry",
        "maths",
        "cheatsheet",
        "sohcahtoa"
      ],
      "slides": [
        {
          "layout": "formula",
          "eyebrow": "maths · save this 📌",
          "title": "Trigonometry cheat sheet",
          "cells": [
            {
              "name": "SOH CAH TOA",
              "f": "sin θ = {O // H}   cos θ = {A // H}   tan θ = {O // A}",
              "wide": true
            },
            {
              "name": "Pythagoras",
              "f": "a^{2} + b^{2} = c^{2}",
              "note": "c = hypotenuse"
            },
            {
              "name": "area of any triangle",
              "f": "{1 // 2}ab sin C"
            },
            {
              "name": "sine rule",
              "f": "{a // sin A} = {b // sin B} = {c // sin C}",
              "note": "use with a side–angle pair",
              "wide": true
            },
            {
              "name": "cosine rule",
              "f": "a^{2} = b^{2} + c^{2} − 2bc cos A",
              "note": "use with 3 sides, or 2 sides + the angle between them",
              "wide": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
